"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":0.08891533398598228,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.09143150584437815,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.00681,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":4.5,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Travere Therapeutics, Inc., a biopharmaceutical company, identifies, develops, and delivers therapies to people living with rare kidney and metabolic diseases in the United States. The company's products include FILSPARI (sparsentan), a once-daily, oral medication designed to target two critical pathways in the disease progression of IgA Nephropathy (endothelin 1 and angiotensin-II); and Thiola and Thiola EC (tiopronin tablets) for the treatment of cystinuria, a rare genetic cystine transport disorder that causes high cystine levels in the urine and the formation of recurring kidney stones. Its clinical-stage programs consist of Sparsentan, a novel investigational product candidate, which has been granted Orphan Drug Designation for the treatment of focal segmental glomerulosclerosis in the U.S. and Europe; and Pegtibatinase, a novel investigational human enzyme replacement candidate being evaluated for the treatment of classical homocystinuria. It has a collaboration agreement with PharmaKrysto Limited for the pre-clinical activities associated with the cystinuria program. Travere Therapeutics, Inc. was formerly known as Retrophin, Inc. and changed its name to Travere Therapeutics, Inc. in November 2020. The company is headquartered in San Diego, California.","ceo_bio":"Dr. Eric M. Dube Ph.D. | President, CEO & Director | Age 52 | Compensation: $1.8M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 497 people. Revenue per employee of $987K ranks in the top quartile among Healthcare peers. Stock-based compensation of $90K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Travere Therapeutics, Inc. is a mid-cap healthcare business with a $4.8B market cap on $491M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +32% over the past three years and +17% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -23% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","Accruals are elevated at -10.5% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, thin -5.8\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Operating margins 13% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 860% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":8.602895752895755},{"text":"Elevated short interest (14.8% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $50.0M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 15% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.3% return)","Healthcare tends to hold up well as investors rotate into defensive names"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Contrasting Travere Therapeutics (NASDAQ:TVTX) and InflaRx (NASDAQ:IFRX)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/05/contrasting-travere-therapeutics-nasdaqtvtx-and-inflarx-nasdaqifrx.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793901766.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.934,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Guggenheim Has Lowered Expectations for Travere Therapeutics (NASDAQ:TVTX) Stock Price","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/04/guggenheim-has-lowered-expectations-for-travere-therapeutics-nasdaqtvtx-stock-price.html","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793806249.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.421,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"The Technical Signals Behind (TVTX) That Institutions Follow","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/9/The_Technical_Signals_Behind_TVTX_That_Institutions_Follow_1